# Removed from the Ubuntu Server cloud image.
#
# Server images carry no GUI, so this list is not about the desktop -- it is
# about every remaining path a human has to a prompt that is not the agent.
# One package per line; '#' comments and blanks ignored.

# --- interactive login surfaces -------------------------------------------
# (getty binaries stay: the break-glass path needs agetty. What goes is the
#  machinery that presents a login to anyone who did not ask for rescue.)

# --- cloud-init stays, deliberately ----------------------------------------
# An earlier version of this file said cloud-init was purged after first boot
# and pointed at a build-rootfs.sh that does not exist. It was never removed.
#
# It is now load-bearing on EVERY boot: bootcmd masks the gettys before
# getty.target is reached, which is the only hook early enough to stop the
# provisioning boot printing a login prompt. Keeping it is a decision, not an
# oversight -- with the cost stated plainly: cloud-init executes whatever its
# datasource says, so anyone who can attach a CIDATA volume gets root without
# going through the agent.

# --- interactive helpers with no meaning on an agent-only box --------------
ubuntu-advantage-tools
landscape-common
update-notifier-common
motd-news-config
byobu
screen
tmux
command-not-found
bash-completion

# --- documentation nobody will read from a machine with no pager -----------
man-db
manpages
info
